flowchart TB
  accTitle: Upward clock search and a single backoff after instability
  accDescr: AutoOC uses finite rungs and higher-voltage retries. Any fresh or cached unsafe point allows at most one lower-clock ceiling backoff, then ends the climb.
  INPUT([OC / clock reclaim<br/>or a higher custom target]) --> LADDER["Build ≤10 unique main rungs<br/>Editable V; fixed target ceilings"]
  LADDER --> NEXT{"Another legal main rung?"}
  NEXT -->|No| PICK
  NEXT -->|Yes| CACHE{"Fresh blacklist<br/>blocks this pair?"}
  CACHE -->|Yes| BACKOFF
  CACHE -->|No| PROBE["Apply / read back<br/>Probe the complete curve"]
  PROBE --> OUTCOME{"Outcome"}
  OUTCOME -->|Pass| WALL{"Confirmed power wall?"}
  WALL -->|No: keep passing evidence| NEXT
  WALL -->|Yes: end climb| PICK
  OUTCOME -->|Fresh UNSAFE| BACKOFF["At most one backoff candidate<br/>Earlier passing MHz<br/>Highest allowed ladder voltage<br/>Probe only an allowed pair"]
  BACKOFF -->|Any ordinary outcome: end climb| PICK
  OUTCOME -->|RECOVERABLE rejection| RETRY["Retry same MHz at next higher V<br/>Finite bins below the ceiling<br/>Recheck cache; apply and probe"]
  RETRY -->|Probe result| OUTCOME
  RETRY -->|Cached UNSAFE| BACKOFF
  RETRY -->|None remain| NEXT
  OUTCOME -->|Critical error / user stop| HALT([Stop probing<br/>Keep completed profiles])
  BACKOFF -->|Critical error / user stop| HALT
  PICK([End climb<br/>Select an eligible passing curve<br/>Continue to final selection])
  classDef setup fill:#19334b,stroke:#84c7f5,color:#edf5fa,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef work fill:#18382f,stroke:#80d9ac,color:#edf5fa,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef gate fill:#302c20,stroke:#e9bd76,color:#fff0d8,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef stop fill:#40252a,stroke:#ef9595,color:#fff0f0,stroke-width:1.5px
  class INPUT,LADDER setup
  class PROBE,PICK work
  class NEXT,CACHE,OUTCOME,WALL,BACKOFF,RETRY gate
  class HALT stop
